question:
A 50 Hz, 275 kV line of length 400 km has the following parameters:

Resistance, $R = 0.035 \ \Omega/\text{km}$;
Inductance, $L = 1 \text{ mH}/\text{km}$;
Capacitance, $C = 0.01 \ \mu\text{F}/\text{km}$;

The line is represented by the nominal-$\pi$ model. With the magnitudes of the sending end and the receiving end voltages of the line (denoted by $V_S$ and $V_R$, respectively) maintained at 275 kV, the phase angle difference ($\theta$) between $V_S$ and $V_R$ required for maximum possible active power to be delivered to the receiving end, in degree is ________ (Round off to 2 decimal places).
